  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is the first PR for #1120. It adds a guard and changes no colour.\n\n- New test file `crates/ui/tests/colour_literals.rs`. It walks `crates/ui/src` and counts the colour literals in each file that is not a test file (`tests.rs`, `*_tests.rs`, `tests/`). A colour literal is a named constant such as `Color32::WHITE`, or a constructor whose arguments are all numbers written in place, such as `Color32::from_rgb(245, 240, 250)`, also across lines. A constructor over variables (`from_rgb(r, g, b)`) converts a colour chosen elsewhere and does not count. `Color32::TRANSPARENT` does not count. A line comment does not count.\n- Each count must equal its row in `ALLOWED`:\n  - a file with a new literal, or a file with no row, fails: \"read a theme token instead\";\n  - a file with fewer literals fails until its row is lowered or removed. Thus the list only shrinks.\n- Each row says why:\n  - `keep:` for a colour that is not a choice for a theme: the token tables, the contrast maths, and a colour that only measures text;\n  - `move (#1120 <family>)` for a site that a later PR moves to theme tokens.\n- On `main` at f287a370c the list has 24 files and 142 literals. About 105 of them are sites to move (the 2026-11-12 estimate said 51).\n- The guard does not see colour data kept as plain numbers: the G-code syntax table in `gcode_highlight.rs` (tuples) and `[u8; 3]` consts such as `PICK_RGB8`. The family PRs move those by name.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1120-colour-literal-guard.md`.\n\n## The plan after this PR\n\nOne PR for each family. Each adds its tokens to `Tokens` (dark and light tables) and to the theme-file keys (`theme_files::COLOR_NAMES`), moves the sites, and lowers its rows. Each is `Refs #1120`. The last one is `Fixes #1120`.\n\n1. Viewport overlays: pick, avoid and handle inks, ground ink, view cube, viewport bar, generate overlay, drop hint, shell overlays.\n2. Tool drawings: tool, holder and profile previews, tool library views.\n3. Verdict palettes (`colorvision.rs`): into the token table, values unchanged, as the issue says.\n4. G-code syntax colours, window chrome and status inks.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows`: the guard. A failure prints today's counts in the row format.\n  - With one literal added to `egui_app/error_text.rs`, it fails with `egui_app/error_text.rs: 2 colour literals, the row allows 1: read a theme token instead`.\n  - With one `Color32::WHITE` in `egui_app/window_chrome.rs` replaced by `Color32::TRANSPARENT`, it fails with `egui_app/window_chrome.rs: 1 colour literals, the row says 2: lower the row to 1`.\n- `colour_literals::the_rows_are_sorted_and_each_says_why`.\n- `colour_literals::the_counter_sees_each_form_and_skips_comments`: the counter on a fixed text, with a constructor split over lines and two conversions of variables that must not count.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the head 7614c70db (two commits: the guard, then the stricter counter):\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 1 step (`ui suites: colour_literals`), 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps -p camcraft-ui --test colour_literals -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `rustfmt --check` on the new file: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: 0 steps reached).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No change to the app. The guard reads source files only.\n- A literal written through a `use` alias (for example `use egui::Color32 as C`) is not counted. No such alias is in `crates/ui` today.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nBranch made from `upstream/main` at f287a370c.\n\nRefs #1120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
